  number={},
  pages={736-739},
  abstract={In the medical field, segmentation of dental images is of significant importance. In this paper,we present a two-stage segmentation framework based on V-Net for the precise segmentation of teeth in dental CBCT images. The proposed framework consists of two stages: First, a region-of-interest (ROI) extraction network is used to localize the tooth regions, thereby reducing computational complexity. Second, a root and tooth mask prediction network is utilized to perform fine tooth segmentation. Experimental results demonstrate that this method outperforms traditional approaches using U-Net and V-Net alone in terms of segmentation accuracy and efficiency, effectively enhancing the accuracy and robustness of tooth segmentation. Comparisons with existing methods further validate the superiority of the proposed approach in the field of dental image segmentation.},
  keywords={Deep learning;Image segmentation;Accuracy;Teeth;Network architecture;Robustness;Dentistry;Data mining;Information technology;Biomedical imaging;Dental CBCT Image Segmentation;V-Net;Two-Stage Segmentation Framework;ROI Extraction;Tooth Mask Prediction;Deep Learning},
